SUMMARY:Watch Party: Kentucky Derby
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: Sports & Games\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: Avail
 able\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/180914\n\nWhat’
 s better than cheering on your horse with a Mint Julep in hand? Doing it f
 rom the comfort of The Pub—soaking up all the Derby Day buzz and countin
 g down to the 6:57PM post time without missing a moment of the action.\n\n
 We’re bringing Churchill Downs to the ‘House with a Derby celebration 
 featuring classic Mint Juleps\, and inspired cocktails - the Royal Julep\,
  and Derby Flower. In addition enjoy an à la carte Derby-inspired menu of
  bites by the chef. Members are encouraged to wear daytime cocktail attire
 . Hats are optional—however highly encouraged. \n\n*Menu specials begin 
 at 4:00PM. Reservations are not required\, however recommended. Following 
 our usual policy\, members are allowed to bring up to three guests to this
  occasion. \n\nMake a Reservation.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/180914
CATEGORIES:Sports & Games
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-183255@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260503T164500Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260503T164500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260503T190000
SUMMARY:Sunday Screening & Discussion: Any Day Now
LOCATION:The Living Room
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEvent U
 RL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/183255\n\n4:45PM Doors Open\, 
 5:00PM Screening\, 6:30PM Discussion\nFrom writer and director Eric Aronso
 n\, join us for an exclusive screening and conversation featuring Any Day
  Now\, the Boston Film Festival’s Audience Favorite Feature\, offered t
 o ‘Quin members ahead of its wide release on May 5th.\n\nSet against a s
 tory close to home\, the film draws inspiration from the infamous Isabella
  Stewart Gardner Museum heist\, weaving a compelling narrative of ambition
 \, loyalty\, and the consequences of the choices we make. Any Day Now fo
 llows Steve\, a night watchman in his early 20s whose life is already begi
 nning to unravel—his band is falling apart\, debt is mounting\, and he�
 �s entangled in a complicated love. When the enigmatic Marty Lyons pulls h
 im into a world of misfits and moral gray areas\, Steve is forced to confr
 ont whether he’s found a way forward—or set himself on a path to ruin.
 \n\nFilmed and produced entirely in Massachusetts\, this independent film 
 offers a distinctly local lens on a story that blends grit\, intrigue\, an
 d emotional depth.\n\nFollowing the screening\, members are invited to sta
 y for an intimate talkback with Eric Aronson\, offering insight into the c
 reative process\, the film’s local ties\, and his innovative\, Webby-nom
 inated marketing campaign that brought Any Day Now to the screen.\n\n*Th
 is event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Theatre fare and 
 refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/183255
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
