BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-182100@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260508T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260508T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260508T183000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: Finding Justice with New England Innocence Project
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEve
 nt URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/182100\n\n5:00PM Reception
 \, 5:30PM Discussion\nAn evening that will challenge what you think you kn
 ow about justice - and redefine what it means to rebuild a life.\n\nHear f
 irsthand from Sean Ellis and Edward Wright—two men who were wrongfully c
 onvicted\, spent decades incarcerated\, and ultimately fought to reclaim t
 heir freedom. Their stories are deeply personal\, but also powerful reflec
 tions on systemic failure\, resilience\, and the long road to exoneration.
 \n\nSean Ellis\, whose case gained international attention through the Net
 flix docuseries Trial 4\, now leads advocacy efforts through the Exoneree
  Network\, supporting others navigating life after incarceration. Edward W
 right\, exonerated after 41 years\, taught himself the law while imprisone
 d - successfully fighting for his own freedom while helping others do the 
 same.\n\nThe conversation will be guided by Radha Natarajan\, Executive Di
 rector of the New England Innocence Project\, whose work continues to conf
 ront bias and drive meaningful reform within the justice system.\n\nA rare
  opportunity to engage with voices at the forefront of justice reform - an
 d to witness the strength\, clarity\, and humanity behind these extraordin
 ary journeys.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members onl
 y. Light bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/182100
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
